Kernel (SiliconForest 0e1f46661376 + the M3 tree patch), asahi-m3 G15: module parameter
asahi.g15_perf_tgt_util (percent, 30..95; 0 = default = unchanged) for the firmware DVFS target
utilization. The G15S HardwareData template carries perf_tgt_utilization = 80 and
perf_tgt_utilization_2 = 80 at HardwareDataA +0x788 / +0x7ec (template +0x4d08 / +0x4d6c). The offsets
are the G15C record layout (g15/board/record.rs) shifted by HardwareDataA (+0x4580); the fixed
neighbours that record.rs also writes (6, 1 at +0x7a0; 95.0 at +0x7c8) sit at the same shift in the
template, which confirms the layout. The override is written after the template hash check and is
refused unless both words read 80. Neighbouring values for reference: boost min util 90, boost step 50,
filter a 0.2 / a2 0.005, integral gain 1.755, proportional gain 5.85, base pstate 1, max pstate 8.
Why: in stop-and-go loads (the metal-stress pattern: wait and CPU check every 10th frame) the GPU is
busy about half the time, so the firmware lowers the clock to state 1 (338 MHz) to reach 80 % busy.
Built 2026-10-27 (image sha256 3f032b51...); NOT TESTED YET (needs install/stage-n-tgt-util.sh and one boot).
Test plan: boot with asahi.g15_perf_tgt_util=50; check "DVFS target utilization 50 %" in the kernel log;
tests/g1-cpu-side.sh 60 (3 x 60 s per CPU setting) with the pstate sampler; target >= 120 G in the
macOS pattern; then tests/gpu-perf-suite.sh 60 (no change expected in steady loads), idle power on
battery for 10 min against the default, 0 GPU faults. Remove the argument if it does not help.

